 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259482 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259482 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186258796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259482 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fefce3eb-55ec-5c40-a1e4-1147a9146a22" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186257417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186257425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186258113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186258253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186258475 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259483 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259483 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259483 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186257425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259483 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ffcc488d-5039-58c5-9ed9-42126f86d743" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259547 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259547 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123737" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259547 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259547 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [2,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.$ Further, let \n\n$$\nI={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\,\\le I\\,\\le U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and \n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\n$$\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259547 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4c92a16d-8ec0-5bb7-a1d3-67db8dee714c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259547 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $U(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}=f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}\n$$\n\nand the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $3{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259549 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259549 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123741" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259549 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259549 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [-2,-1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=10+y-3x.$ Further, let \n\n$$\nI={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\,\\le I\\,\\le U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and \n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\n$$\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259549 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8df0d876-87f5-5ec6-b4ea-583e00a0fa95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259549 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $U(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)=10+y-3x$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=10+y-3x$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}=f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}\n$$\n\nand the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $10+{y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259550 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259550 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123742" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259550 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259550 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[1,2]\\times [2,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y.$ Further, let \n\n$$\nI={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\,\\le I\\,\\le U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and \n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\n$$\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259550 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2de9d676-815f-5c88-935f-91c621a59e79" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259550 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $L(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}=f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})={x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}\n$$\n\nand the lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259568 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259568 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123839" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259568 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259568 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[-1,3]\\times [2,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=-3$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259568 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "089ded76-3ed3-5ada-805a-37477a513dd6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259568 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=-3,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(-3)\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =-3({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =-3(3-(-1))(5-2) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=-36\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le -36=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=-36.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259569 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259569 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123843" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259569 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259569 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[-5,-2]\\times [3,7]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=1$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259569 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bde095b1-d9b2-5272-b46e-003fde137023" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259569 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=1,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}1\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =(-2-(-5))(7-3) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=12\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le 12=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=12.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259570 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259570 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123846" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259570 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259570 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[1,7]\\times [4,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_